card.statement:
[<<cite:h-s_unit>>] Let $A$ be a square complex matrix such that $A^2$ is normal. Then $A$ is unitarily similar to

- [(a)] a direct sum of blocks, each of which is

\begin{equation}
\begin{bmatrix} \lambda
\end{bmatrix}\ \text{ or
}\
\begin{bmatrix}
\mu & r\\ 0&-\mu
\end{bmatrix},\qquad
\begin{matrix}
\lambda,\mu\in\mathbb
C,\
0\le \arg(\mu)<\pi,\\
r\in\mathbb R,\ r>0;
\end{matrix}
\end{equation}

and

- [(b)] to a direct sum of blocks, each of which is

\begin{equation}
\begin{bmatrix} \lambda
\end{bmatrix}\ \text{ or
}\
\tau\!\begin{bmatrix}
0 & 1\\ \nu&0
\end{bmatrix}
,\qquad
\begin{matrix}
\lambda, \nu \in
\mathbb C,\ |\nu|<1,\\
\tau\in \mathbb R,\
\tau>0.
\end{matrix}
\end{equation}

These direct sums are uniquely determined by $A$, up to permutation of summands. Conversely, if $A$ is unitarily similar to a direct sum of blocks of the form <<ref:s1>> or <<ref:s2>>, then $A^2$ is normal.
